<title>UK: Singer &amp; Friedlander raises 1996 profit.</title>
<headline>Singer &amp; Friedlander raises 1996 profit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			  (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr pre-excep (pence)    11.63		vs 9.96</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		  17.96		vs 10.35</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)   4.65		 vs 4.00</p>
<p> Pretax pre-excep	   41.66		vs 34.19</p>
<p> Pretax			 54.81		vs 34.92</p>
<p> Operating profit	   41.66		vs 34.19</p>
<p> Exceptional profit	 13.15		vs 0.735</p>
<p>Full company name - Singer &amp; Friedlander Plc.</p>
<p>Note - The exceptional profit in the 1996 accounts refers mainly to the sale of the company's shareholding in Peoples Phone and associated goodwill net of the loss on the sale of insurance broker Edgar Hamilton.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8864.</p>
</text>
